y**\n   - **Fact:** Mercury has no atmosphere, so it experiences extreme temperature swings. Daytime temperatures can reach 800°F (430°C), while nighttime temperatures can drop to -290°F (-180°C).\n\n2. **Venus**\n   - **Fact:** Venus rotates in the opposite direction to most other planets (retrograde rotation). A day on Venus (one full rotation) is longer than its year (one orbit around the Sun).\n\n3. **Earth**\n   - **Fact:** Earth is the only planet known to have liquid water on its surface and is the only one with a global magnetic field strong enough to protect life from harmful solar radiation.\n\n4. **Mars**\n   - **Fact:** Mars has the largest volcano in the solar system, Olympus Mons. It is nearly three times the height of Mount Everest and has a base diameter of about 600 kilometers.\n\n5. **Jupiter**\n   - **Fact:** Jupiter has a storm called the Great Red Spot, which has been raging for at least 350 years.", "client": {"ttft_s": 0.6332368000003044, "decode_s": 4.733447400001751, "total_s": 5.3669808999984525, "n_gen": 256, "n_chunks": 256, "tg": 53.87194119869287, "pp": 41.0588898181336}}
